{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Post-hoist Ubuntu evidence from Gerrit change 1756, Verified run 31763574312 (still waiting on macOS; all three Ubuntu cells green). The bridge cadence test disappeared from every Ubuntu slowest-25 list, confirming its 100.66-130.59s baseline per-test attribution is eliminated. The only remaining individual Ubuntu pytest operation over 30s is the provenance-analysis session setup: 48.67s on py3.11, 51.48s on py3.12, and 55.60s on py3.13. Default-suite walls were 599.54s, 650.26s, and 647.20s versus baseline 615s, 634s, and 563s; the summed wall increased 85s, so this single run does not support a runner-release claim despite eliminating the repeated YAML work. The successor long pole plus aggregate suite/runtime variance dominate. This distinction will remain explicit: local boundary savings and per-test removal are proven; Ubuntu job-wall savings are not yet proven. Integrations were 82.83s, 92.06s, and 87.28s, with no individual test over 30s."},"env_id":"0993f6a8-7a6a-4707-a671-c5bbb2691444","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786675208096556001,"uuid":"8574ffe0-bec4-40ed-9669-84c967ee255e"}